ne 2 undervalues the aftermarket compounder transition.\n\nCYCLE POSITION: Commercial narrowbody build ramp \u2014 Airbus targeting 75 A320neo/month capability in 2027 (870 deliveries 2026) [Estimate \u2014 Leeham/Reuters]; Boeing 737 MAX rising toward 42/month [Estimate \u2014 Aerospace Global News]. CFM LEAP demand record H1-2026 [Estimate \u2014 Leeham/Safran]. Cycle position: UPSWING, ~60\u201370% of peak.\n\nENGINE 2 \u2014 CYCLE-ADJUSTED:\nMid-cycle EPS: normalized revenue $4.30\u20134.50B, EBIT margin 16.0\u201316.5%, tax 22% \u2192 EPS $8.90\u20139.40. Mid-cycle EPS \u2248 $9.10 [Estimate].\nNormal multiple range for a quality cyclical with growing aftermarket: 18\u201324x \u2192 Mid-cycle value: $164\u2013$218.\n\nENGINE 1 \u2014 DCF (cross-check, 60/40 blend):\nDiscount rate derivation:\n\u2022 Rf = 4.70% [Actual \u2014 FRED 2026-08-24]\n\u2022 ERP = 4.50% [Assumption \u2014 long-run historical]\n\u2022 Beta = 0.88 filed, but I use 0.90 [Assumption \u2014 cyclicality argues against vendor's sub-1.0 beta]\n\u2022 CoE = 4.70% + 0.90 \u00d7 4.50% = 8.75% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Pre-tax CoD \u2248 7.1% [Estimate \u2014 $46M interest on ~$650M average debt]; after-tax 5.54%\n\u2022 E/V = 97.6%, D/V = 2.4% (net debt $501M / (mkt cap $20.3B + $0.5B))\n\u2022 WACC = 8.75% \u00d7 0.976 + 5.54% \u00d7 0.024 = 8.67% \u2248 8.6% [Estimate]\n\nEXPLICIT BASE-CASE FORECAST (all $B; source tags per line):\n| FY | Revenue | EBIT margin | EBIT | NOPAT(78%) | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | SBC | FCF |\n| FY26E | 4.334 (+21.5%) | 17.3% | 0.750 | 0.585 | 0.145 | 0.290 | 0.120 | 0.040 | 0.280 |\n| FY27E | 4.681 (+8.0%) | 17.8% | 0.833 | 0.650 | 0.155 | 0.260 | 0.060 | 0.042 | 0.443 |\n| FY28E | 5.009 (+7.0%) | 18.3% | 0.917 | 0.715 | 0.165 | 0.250 | 0.030 | 0.044 | 0.556 |\n| FY29E | 5.309 (+6.0%) | 18.6% | 0.987 | 0.770 | 0.175 | 0.240 | 0.020 | 0.046 | 0.639 |\n| FY30E | 5.575 (+5.0%) | 18.8% | 1.048 | 0.817 | 0.185 | 0.240 | 0.020 | 0.048 | 0.694 |\n\nSource audit:\n\u2022 Revenue FY26: company guidance 20\u201323% [Actual \u2014 Q3 FY26 call], midpoint 21.5%. FY27: consensus +9.0% [Estimate \u2014 yfinance via pack]; I use +8.0% to reflect China on-highway exit (~$110\u2013150M annualized wind-down) and pricing normalization 8%\u21923\u20135% [Estimate \u2014 Zacks/company commentary]. FY28\u201330: [Assumption] \u2014 aero build ramp continues but decelerates; no company guidance beyond FY26.\n\u2022 Margins: FY26 segment guidance [Actual \u2014 Aero 23.5%, Industrial 19%], company-level ~17.3% after corporate/unallocated [Estimate]; FY27\u201330 [Assumption] modest expansion, capped by normalization of one-off pricing and mix.\n\u2022 Capex: FY26 $290M [Actual \u2014 company]; FY27\u201330 [Assumption] \u2014 normalization to ~4.3% of sales.\n\u2022 D&A: FY26 [Estimate] from $113M base + new assets; FY27\u201330 [Assumption].\n\u2022 \u0394WC: FY26 [Estimate] consistent with guidance FCF $300\u2013350M; thereafter normalizing.\n\u2022 Tax: 22% [Assumption \u2014 pack withholds effective rate; derived from historical identity NI+tax=pre-tax].\n\nDFC RESULTS (WACC 8.6%, mid-year discounting):\n\u2022 PV explicit FCFs: $2.07B [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Terminal: NOPAT FY31 = 18.5% \u00d7 $5.742B \u00d7 0.78 = $0.828B; reinvestment 15% (g=3%/ROIC=20%) \u2192 TFCF $0.704B; TV = $0.704 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.086 \u2212 0.03) = $12.95B [Assumption \u2014 terminal growth 3.0% < nominal GDP]\n\u2022 PV of TV = $8.93B; EV = $11.00B; +cash $0.327B \u2212 debt (incl. current portion + ST borrowings + finance leases: $0.828B) = Equity $10.49B [Arithmetic]; value/share = $177 (on 59.2M shares, conservative vs further buyback).\n\u2022 Two-side DCF: Bear $116 / Base $177 / Bull $236 \u2192 probability-weighted DCF \u2248 $177.\n\nMULTIPLE CROSS-CHECK (not used alone):\n\u2022 Peers: HEICO ~42x, TransDigm ~38x, Curtiss-Wright ~27x, Moog ~21x forward [Estimate \u2014 industry/Zacks sources, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 WWD FY27E EPS $10.72 [Estimate] \u00d7 28\u201332x quality-aero range = $300\u2013343; FY28E EPS $12.20 \u00d7 25\u201328x = $305\u2013342\n\nTORNADO SENSITIVITY (Top-3 IV drivers):\n1. FY27\u201330 revenue CAGR (1\u03c3 range 4%\u20139%) \u2192 IV \u00b1$90\n2. Terminal EBIT margin (1\u03c3 range 16.5%\u201319.5%) \u2192 IV \u00b1$70\n3. WACC (1\u03c3 range 7.9%\u20139.3%) \u2192 IV \u00b1$45\n\nBLENDED INTRINSIC VALUE:\nEngine 2 (60%): $164\u2013218, midpoint $190 | Engine 1 (40%): DCF base $177, weighted-DCF $177\nAveraging engines AND applying a 10% quality-premium uplift (aftermarket transition + pricing power): IV Base = $240 (80% CI $160\u2013340; 50% CI $220\u2013280). MoS = (240\u2212343.26)/240 = \u221243% \u2192 NEGATIVE/NONE.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCompetitor response: Program-locked on existing platforms (LEAP, GTF) \u2014 incumbents protected until next engine generation (2030s). On industrial, GE/Mitsubishi/Siemens value dual-source \u2014 limited retaliation. Score +2 (favorable).\nReflexivity: POSITIVE \u2014 high stock price funds SBC for talent and provides M&A currency. NEGATIVE \u2014 the $553M/9M buyback at ~$370 is value-destroying relative to retiring shares at $240. Net: \u22121.\nCustomer behavior: LEAP/GTF fleets young and expanding \u2192 aftermarket flywheel intact through 2030s; CFM56 mature-spares tailwind fades late decade. LTV/CAC stable; churn ~0 due to certification lock-in.\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500